  "term": "beta-secretase",
  "definition": "Beta-secretase, specifically the enzyme BACE1, cuts amyloid precursor protein in a way that increases production of beta-amyloid. In Alzheimer’s disease, this process is linked to amyloid plaque buildup between neurons, which can disrupt neural signaling and contribute to memory impairment.",
